"""Advanced board-level repair guides (own words): micro-soldering, hot air rework, reading schematics, short-circuit and rail diagnosis, charging and backlight circuits, BGA work, liquid damage and trace repair.
These are advanced, practice-heavy skills. The guides say when to stop and refer the job out. Always work on practice boards before a customer's device."""
from app.services.it_repair_phones import g

_ESD = "Work on an anti-static mat with a wrist strap, and disconnect the battery before touching the board. "
_FUME = "Solder with ventilation or a fume extractor, and keep flux and alcohol away from open flame and hot air. "

